The Luxtronik client (src/luxtronik/) and the fake controller of the tests
were written in JavaScript for this project, from the understanding of the
protocol of port 8889 as documented by these projects, all released under
the MIT License: python-luxtronik (https://github.com/Bouni/python-luxtronik:
commands 3002 to 3005, the register indexes, scales and codes, the search
datagram), BenPru/luxtronik (https://github.com/BenPru/luxtronik: the serial
number, the hot water target register by firmware, the scale of the energy
input counters, the firmware V1.90 / V2.90 that crashes on writes, the
detection of hot water and cooling) and TbsJah/ioBroker.luxtronik2-controller
(https://github.com/TbsJah/ioBroker.luxtronik2-controller: read before write,
flash wear, the ports of the WebSocket and Modbus interfaces). No code was copied. The fake controller was checked against
python-luxtronik 0.3.14 (scripts/check-simulator.sh).

